{"name":"Seeing Red","hex":"#d42a3e","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seeing red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of see red"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seeing_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seeing Red (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Seeing Red is the debut album by Canadian pop-punk band LiveonRelease, released by Her Royal Majesty's Records in 2001."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seeing_Red_(album)","wikidata":"Q7445758"},{"title":"Seein' Red (Unwritten Law song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Seein' Red\" is a song by the American rock band Unwritten Law, released as the second single on January 14, 2002 from the band's fourth studio album, Elva, which was released on January 29 of that same year. It was written by singer Scott Russo and produced by Michael \"Miguel\" Happoldt. It became the highest-charting single of the band's career, holding the number one spot on Billboard's Modern Rock Tracks chart for four weeks between May and June 2002. The music video for \"Seein' Red\" was directed by Marc Webb."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Unwritten_Law_-_Seein%27_Red_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seein'_Red_(Unwritten_Law_song)","wikidata":"Q7445740"},{"title":"Seeing Red (Ms. Marvel)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Seeing Red\" is the fourth episode of the American television miniseries Ms. Marvel, based on Marvel Comics featuring the character Ms. Marvel. It follows Kamala Khan as she travels to Karachi, Pakistan to learn more about her mysterious bangle. The episode is set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), sharing continuity with the films of the franchise. It was written by Sabir Pirzada, A. C. Bradley, and Matthew Chauncey, with a story by Pirzada. The episode was directed by Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/Ms._Marvel_%22Seeing_Red%22_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seeing_Red_(Ms._Marvel)","wikidata":"Q112810397"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg/250px-Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg/250px-Liveonrelease-seeingred.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiveonrelease-seeingred.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f0/Unwritten_Law_-_Seein%27_Red_cover.jpg/250px-Unwritten_Law_-_Seein%27_Red_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign